WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.510
Heat and flooding threaten cold-chain reliability.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:08.112
Before committing to a retrofit, investigate what could change your choice.

00:00:08.162 --> 00:00:11.067
I’m Jangho Lee, and this is GEONOS.

00:00:11.374 --> 00:00:16.904
Built during the hackathon: this NYC workspace, evidence pipeline, and six-model workflow.

00:00:16.954 --> 00:00:21.124
Explore all five boroughs and more than a million official outlines.

00:00:21.174 --> 00:00:25.192
Public data and pretrained models remain acknowledged foundations.

00:00:25.488 --> 00:00:29.850
Select 572 Smith Street, then 592.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.036
Their records compare immediately.

00:00:32.086 --> 00:00:37.179
Search, filters, layers, and recorded-height 3D locate candidates;

00:00:37.229 --> 00:00:40.483
tax-lot floor area stays distinct from building measurements.

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:44.872
Require twenty thousand square feet of usable area: unknown.

00:00:44.922 --> 00:00:51.317
Change the measurement to mapped footprint: 572 meets it; 592 does not.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:54.275
That is a checked condition, not a suitability score.

00:00:54.572 --> 00:00:57.320
A blank flood-map point isn’t clearance.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:00.579
DEP models building interiors as voids.

00:01:00.629 --> 00:01:08.692
In its published 2050 scenario, the deep class touches 572’s outline and is about forty-seven meters from 592.

00:01:08.999 --> 00:01:13.667
The next check: survey entrances, drains, and equipment elevations.

00:01:13.717 --> 00:01:20.652
Regional climate projections and station history add context; JFK’s paired weather keeps actual heat and moisture

00:01:20.702 --> 00:01:21.483
together.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.688
Energy has boundaries, too.

00:01:23.738 --> 00:01:29.079
At Lombardy Street, parent and child reports repeat energy but use different areas.

00:01:29.129 --> 00:01:33.025
Request the meter-to-building schedule before judging efficiency.

00:01:33.322 --> 00:01:37.935
Muse Voice turns a sample question into an editable draft.

00:01:37.985 --> 00:01:44.108
Muse Spark orchestrates bounded official-data tools, carrying the user’s goal and source references into the

00:01:44.158 --> 00:01:45.150
conversation.

00:01:45.458 --> 00:01:51.548
SAM 3.1 segments roofs and trees in the actual dated aerial crops.

00:01:51.598 --> 00:01:54.640
Switch between sites and the original imagery.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.108
A missed detection never proves absence.

00:01:57.405 --> 00:02:03.475
Muse Wonder reviews typed summaries, not unseen pixels, and proposes survey targets.

00:02:03.525 --> 00:02:08.904
Map-mask disagreement directs inspection; it is not a condition rating or resilience score.

00:02:08.954 --> 00:02:13.067
Both image analyses completed before Wonder reviewed their summaries.

00:02:13.363 --> 00:02:19.990
DINOv2 runs locally, comparing contextual features in 2020 and 2024 images.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:26.275
Highlighted windows suggest where to look; shadows, season and alignment can also explain differences.

00:02:26.572 --> 00:02:32.812
Muse Image illustrates the inspection plan: what we know, what to verify, and what could change.

00:02:32.862 --> 00:02:37.442
The diagram stays visibly separate from photographs and evidence.

00:02:37.749 --> 00:02:39.789
Sources keep their dates and scope.

00:02:39.839 --> 00:02:43.062
Export the comparison and unresolved requirements.

00:02:43.112 --> 00:02:48.900
If Meta filters a question, the app preserves that refusal and labels any public-data brief.

00:02:49.186 --> 00:02:56.251
GEONOS makes the next step concrete: request roof plans, inspect drainage, verify usable space and power.

00:02:56.301 --> 00:02:59.900
Investigate what could change the choice before choosing a building.
